WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.490 --> 00:00:03.080
Other companies want Cymbal's data.

2
00:00:03.100 --> 00:00:05.865
Suppliers want to see how their products sell.

3
00:00:05.885 --> 00:00:10.600
And a partner wants joint insights, but must never see customer rows.

4
00:00:10.620 --> 00:00:13.587
The old way is to export files, and send copies.

5
00:00:13.607 --> 00:00:16.475
Copies go stale, and they leak.

6
00:00:16.495 --> 00:00:17.850
The new way: share live.

7
00:00:17.870 --> 00:00:19.285
Do not copy.

8
00:00:19.305 --> 00:00:20.460
Think of a library.

9
00:00:20.480 --> 00:00:21.535
You lend the book.

10
00:00:21.555 --> 00:00:24.220
You do not print a new one for every reader.

11
00:00:24.240 --> 00:00:26.045
Analytics Hub works like that.

12
00:00:26.065 --> 00:00:28.555
It is now called BigQuery sharing.

13
00:00:28.575 --> 00:00:30.830
You publish a listing in an exchange.

14
00:00:30.850 --> 00:00:34.265
The subscriber gets a linked dataset, read only.

15
00:00:34.285 --> 00:00:35.640
No data is copied.

16
00:00:35.660 --> 00:00:37.040
It is always current.

17
00:00:37.060 --> 00:00:40.440
And the subscriber pays for their own queries.

18
00:00:40.460 --> 00:00:43.050
And the partner who must not see rows?

19
00:00:43.070 --> 00:00:44.537
Use a data clean room.

20
00:00:44.557 --> 00:00:46.163
Both sides bring data.

21
00:00:46.183 --> 00:00:49.285
Only combined, aggregated answers come out.

22
00:00:49.305 --> 00:00:53.670
And egress controls on a listing can block copying and exporting.

23
00:00:53.690 --> 00:00:59.470
The trap: scheduled exports to partners, when a live listing avoids copies.

24
00:00:59.490 --> 00:01:00.730
Recap.

25
00:01:00.750 --> 00:01:02.480
Share live with Analytics Hub.

26
00:01:02.500 --> 00:01:05.565
And use a clean room when rows must stay hidden.

27
00:01:05.585 --> 00:01:06.652
Line four, done.

28
00:01:06.672 --> 00:01:09.385
Try the checkpoint below.
